{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Unto the young woman there is no sin worthy of death.</b> Even though she ultimately submitted willingly, since the matter began under coercion she is exempt — for since it began under forbidden compulsion, her passion overpowered her, as the Sages said (Ketubot 51a): ״אֲפִילּוּ אוֹמֶרֶת הַנִּיחוּ לוֹ כוּ׳״ (Even if she says, 'Leave him…')." "<b>For as when a man rises against his fellow, etc.</b> This is not like the case of the beast that is written ״וְאֶת הַבְּהֵמָה תַּהֲרֹגוּ״ (Leviticus 20:15), for the beast did not resist at all; but this one, whose case began under coercion yet resisted as best she could — what happened to her is like what happened to the murdered victim in whom a transgression was carried out against his will. Therefore the sin has no relevance to her at all."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:02.659694834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}